{"contract":"translation_contextual_v2","candidate_identity":"1de4f2bac0a176982199b5eb5efb45d1bc63a766521af264bca744f8074b672d","verdicts":[{"revision_key":"12ff2c09d3bbb8e88b78439e0cdea8bf0652d9ffc9866add320012f2524a954d","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"e00b2a8b68e9b6787d6fc7a22b4b62a97c32ec7146ec7b71575097516df05ce7","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"e8fc5b0a4a9d6c3e85ebcbf79ddc5b41a7e1b2c8d28b1a47d34440af8167e8a2","verdict":"ISSUE","observation":"The source (cursed.lua:22, description of the endless hunt talent type) says \"Each day, you lift your weary body and begin the unending hunt\": every day you drag your worn-out body up and start the hunt again. The translation 「你不知疲倦无时无刻狩猎你的下一个目标」 means \"you tirelessly hunt your next target at every moment\". That turns weary (exhausted) into its opposite (tireless). It also drops \"each day\" and the image of lifting a tired body, and it adds \"your next target\", which is not in the source."},{"revision_key":"e90949f9259fbaa1b4aeb7bbdef559ace4df0d4539c8c53e005c3d8c9dd5d43c","verdict":"ISSUE","observation":"The source is the achievement name \"Dreaming my dreams\" (quests.lua:338). Its desc at line 340 is \"Experienced and completed all the dreams in the Dogroth Caldera\", so the name means the player dreamed their own dreams. The translation 「我的梦就是你的梦」 means \"my dreams are your dreams\". It changes the statement into an equation between two people and adds a \"you\" that the source does not have, so the achievement's meaning drifts. A rendering along the lines of 「做着我的梦」 would keep it."},{"revision_key":"e92433bcbaf2d4dc438a1651a4cb5214c7e4c8dae5438f8418253e0e829740af","verdict":"ISSUE","observation":"Line-break mismatch: the source has 12 newlines and the translation has 13. Source line 23 (unlock-yeek.lua) is a single sentence, but the translation splits it into two lines at 「……样子有点滑稽。\\n不过他们是……」, which changes the paragraph layout. Minor, in the same sentence: \"cunning\" is rendered 「灵巧」 (nimble, deft), which is not the same as the source's meaning of shrewd or crafty."},{"revision_key":"e9253668295a71c738227e4186efa5e9fa86c30ccc629240168490030d584083","verdict":"ISSUE","observation":"Second stanza of the poem (misc.lua:536-539). \"Once flowers rose to reach the sky\" is rendered 「曾经炽热的复仇火焰染红天空」 (\"the once-blazing fire of revenge stained the sky red\"), which has nothing to do with the source. The flowers-reaching-the-sky image is gone, and an image of vengeful fire is invented. \"Now all lost, now all fled\" is rendered 「今为尘土，今为虚无」 (\"now dust, now nothingness\"), which just repeats the first stanza's \"All is dust, all is dead\" and loses the meaning of lost and fled. Minor: \"Once blossoms fell from beech on high\" says nothing about the flowers being in full bloom, and it drops the beech tree."},{"revision_key":"e928ce2cd082f9a66e9a1d8953272766ee8fd25a91db43afaeb15c4ce337e6a4","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"e95173943342a9e768bab3bcbc0709b0fdc636b0973da55b20e3435d18206041","verdict":"ISSUE","observation":"The source (blight.lua:212) says Numbing Blight \"reduces all damage dealt by %d%%\": the target deals less damage. The translation 「降低 %d%% 伤害」 drops both \"dealt\" and \"all\", so the reader cannot tell whether the damage the target deals goes down or the damage it takes goes down. Read the second way, the debuff could be mistaken for damage reduction on the target. It should say explicitly that the damage the target deals, i.e. all damage it deals, is reduced by %d%%."},{"revision_key":"e9884825395b8560158bbeb0af351556ef369bf2154122ad9c0b7ef1a035f989","verdict":"ISSUE","observation":"misc.lua:513: \"However this theory may be borne purely from the fanatical delusions of certain wyrmics who have studied the creatures for too long\" means the theory may have come purely from the fanatical delusions of some wyrmics. The translation 「然而这个理论只有那些……龙战士信徒们才会相信」 (\"only those wyrmic devotees would believe this theory\") drops the \"may\" and changes the claim from where the theory came from to who believes it. Also in the same text (line 515), \"The Daikara Pass and surrounding mountain chains\" becomes 「岱卡拉山脉」 (\"the Daikara Mountains\"), which changes the pass into a mountain range and drops the surrounding mountain chains. At line 517, \"newly matured drakes\" becomes 「成年巨龙」 (\"adult great dragons\"), losing \"newly\". At line 513, \"over 40'\" becomes 「能达到40英尺」 (\"can reach 40 feet\"), losing \"over\"."},{"revision_key":"e992e87196f4977ed94fb973b203336fc1e2c3a1c570d4380c61bd752bbcbfea","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"e99aa6d60fabd45212faca9eaa0c90069769b53990cd1ae3c1e33d34f99c28a5","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"e9a9aef25b302395915d645f4b01ba831bcc065cafeaddc1b171b8d5a7fef53a","verdict":"OK"}]}